{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790539626053,"sessionID":"ses_f1b882f77ffebyKXRbssgjp7gn","part":{"id":"prt_0e47a5156001yM7A1qDOx5HH6W","messageID":"msg_0e47a4d6f0017PTy1Dfa6knDDa","sessionID":"ses_f1b882f77ffebyKXRbssgjp7gn","type":"reasoning","text":"This is very revealing:\n\n- 9 seeds max out at max_depth=1 (the very start of the game)\n- 1 seed reaches max_depth=6\n- 1 seed reaches max_depth=7  \n- 1 seed reaches max_depth=8\n- 1 seed reaches max_depth=11\n- 2 seeds reach max_depth=25 and 27\n\nThe vast majority of seeds (9 out of 15) don't even get past depth 1. This is a massive early-game problem.\n\nThe two outlier seeds (7 and 8) that reach Dlvl 25-27 suggest that with the right play, a Healer-Gnome can get quite far. But 9/15 seeds fail immediately.\n\nWhat's happening at Dlvl 1? The Healer starts on the first dungeon level. The early game dangers include:\n- Gnome zombies (seed 1)\n- Starvation (seed 2) \n- Cave spiders (seeds 3, 6)\n- Brown mold (seed 5)\n- Ravens, killer bees, hobbits, little dogs\n\nThe key issue is: the bot is dying on the first level, most of the time. This suggests the early game strategy needs work.\n\nLet me think about what improvements would help:\n\n1. **Better early game weapon acquisition**: The Healer starts with a scalpel. If the bot picks up better weapons it finds, it would survive better.\n\n2. **Prayer usage**: Healers can pray for healing. Using prayer when low on HP could prevent death from starvation or low-HP situations.\n\n3. **Food management**: Eating before starving.\n\n4. **Search for traps**: Avoiding traps that cause death or injury.\n\n5. **Avoiding combat with unfavorable odds**: Running away from fights the bot can't win.\n\nLet me look at the combat module and see what fight_heur does.","time":{"start":1790539616598,"end":1790539626045}}}
