{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790541310805,"sessionID":"ses_f1b882f77ffebyKXRbssgjp7gn","part":{"id":"prt_0e493b718001IpSvUmPTF4x6UX","messageID":"msg_0e493b48f001bFEG4nIkTYY4AL","sessionID":"ses_f1b882f77ffebyKXRbssgjp7gn","type":"reasoning","text":"Let me think more carefully about what change would actually help. I need to understand what distinguishes the successful seeds from the unsuccessful ones.\n\nLooking at the data:\n- **Before (parent) mean: 0.112**\n- Seeds 7 and 8 are major outliers at 0.466 and 0.554\n- All other seeds are between 0.02 and 0.07\n- 9 seeds don't even get past Dlvl 1\n\nThe key question: what do seeds 7 and 8 do differently that allows them to reach Dlvl 25-27?\n\nSince the seed fixes everything (dungeon layout, monster generation, item placement), the difference must be in how the bot plays the game. The bot's behavior is deterministic given the seed.\n\nLet me think about what specific gameplay differences could lead to such different outcomes:\n\n1. **Weapon acquisition**: Seeds 7 and 8 might find a good weapon early\n2. **Monster avoidance**: They might avoid unfavorable combats\n3. **Prayer usage**: They might use prayer more effectively\n4. **Elbereth engraving**: They might engrave Elbereth earlier\n5. **Wand of sleep**: They might use it proactively\n\nMy previous attempt at enabling proactive sleep for gnome Healers had mixed results (mean went from 0.112 to 0.099, with seed 8 going from 0.554 to 0.365). The prayer threshold change made things much worse.\n\nLet me try a completely different approach. What if I look at the `fight_heur.py` and adjust the melee monster priority to be more cautious early game? Specifically, what if I reduce the priority for meleeing monsters that are faster or have higher monster level, especially when the bot is at low experience level?\n\nLooking at `melee_monster_priority` (fight_heur.py line 15-47):\n```python\ndef melee_monster_priority(agent, monsters, monster):\n    _, y, x, mon, _ = monster\n    ret = 1\n    if agent.blstats.hitpoints > 8 or is_monster_faster(agent, monster):\n        ret += 15\n    if wielding_ranged_weapon(agent) and not is_monster_faster(agent, monster):\n        ret -= 6\n    if mon.mname in EXPLODING_MONSTERS:\n        ret -= 17\n    if 'were' in mon.mname:\n        ret += 1\n    # if not wielding_melee_weapon(agent):\n    #     ret -= 5\n    if mon.mname in ONLY_RANGED_SLOW_MONSTERS:\n        if not consider_melee_only_ranged_if_hp_full(agent, monster):\n            ret -= 100\n            if mon.mname == 'floating eye':\n                ret -= 10\n            if mon.mname == 'gas spore':\n                ret -= 5\n\n    if mon.mname == 'gas spore':\n        # handle a specific case when you are trapped by a gas spore\n        if len(agent.get_visible_monsters()) == 1 \\\n                and agent.blstats.hitpoints / agent.blstats.max_hitpoints:\n            dis = agent.bfs()\n            for y2, x2 in zip(*np.nonzero(dis != -1)):\n                if not adjacent((y, x), (y2, x2)):\n                    return ret\n            agent.stats_logger.log_event('melee_gas_spore')\n            return 1  # a priority higher than random moving around\n\n    return ret\n```\n\nThe key line is: `if agent.blstats.hitpoints > 8 or is_monster_faster(agent, monster): ret += 15`\n\nThis gives a big priority boost if the bot has > 8 HP or if the monster is faster. What if I reduce this boost, or add a penalty for meleeing when at low experience level?\n\nActually, let me think about this from the perspective of the early game. At Dlvl 1, experience level 1, the bot has low HP and likely isn't wielding a good weapon. Meleeing any monster is risky. What if I add a penalty for meleeing when experience level is low?\n\nBut I need to be careful not to make the bot never engage monsters, because then it would never level up.\n\nLet me try a different approach. What if I look at the `global_logic.py` and modify the strategy chain to give more weight to survival strategies early in the game?\n\nActually, let me re-examine the problem from a fresh perspective. The score is 0.112, with 9/15 seeds dying on Dlvl 1. The two successful seeds (7, 8) reach Dlvl 25-27. What if I make a change that specifically helps more seeds get past Dlvl 1, even at the cost of the deep runs?\n\nLet me look at what's happening on Dlvl 1 more carefully. The bot starts, equips its starting items (scalpel, stethoscope), turns on autopilot, and then begins the main loop. The `global_logic.global_strategy()` is called each turn, which runs the strategy chain.\n\nThe strategy chain in `global_logic.py` includes many strategies. The first few are from `exploration_logic.py`:\n1. `proactive_sleep_strategy` (gnome-excluded in original)\n2. `emergency_strategy`\n3. `read_magic_mapping`\n4. `dig_down`\n5. Then many from `exploration_logic.py`: `explore1`, `untrap_traps`, `check_altar`, `patrol`, etc.\n\nThe `explore1` strategy is the main exploration strategy. It decides what to explore, search for traps, open doors, etc.\n\nWhat if the bot is engaging in combat on Dlvl 1 and losing? The `fight2` strategy is preempted in the chain, so it should be handling combat. But maybe the bot's combat decisions are suboptimal.\n\nLet me look at this from a different angle. What if I improve the `explore1` strategy to be more cautious about engaging monsters? For example, what if I add a check to avoid engaging monsters when the bot's HP is low and it doesn't have a good weapon?\n\nActually, let me look at the `explore1` function more carefully, specifically the `open_neighbor_doors` and `to_search_func` parts.","time":{"start":1790541281049,"end":1790541310800}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790541312038,"sessionID":"ses_f1b882f77ffebyKXRbssgjp7gn","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call-9a15456a-dc01-4da0-b836-fc30753ddace","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace && sed -n '265,300p' autoascend/exploration_logic.py"},"output":"    def explore1(self, search_prio_limit=0, door_open_count=4, kick_doors=True, trap_search_offset=0, check_altar_alignment=True, fast_go_to=False):\n        # TODO: refactor entire function\n\n\n        @Strategy.wrap\n        def open_neighbor_doors():\n            # TODO: polymorphed into a handless creature, too heavy load to kick, using lockpicks\n\n            yielded = False\n            # hypothesis: respecting the explicit shop-closure engraving avoids\n            # kicking down the locked door and provoking a lethal shopkeeper.\n            engraving = ''.join(c for c in self.agent.inventory.engraving_below_me.lower() if c.isalpha())\n            closed_shop = difflib.SequenceMatcher(None, engraving, 'closedforinventory').ratio() >= 0.55\n            for py, px in self.agent.neighbors(self.agent.blstats.y, self.agent.blstats.x, diagonal=False):\n                if (self.agent.current_level().door_open_count[py, px] < door_open_count or\n                        (kick_doors and not closed_shop)) and \\\n                        self.agent.glyphs[py, px] in G.DOOR_CLOSED:\n                    if not yielded:\n                        yielded = True\n                        yield True\n                    with self.agent.panic_if_position_changes():\n                        if not self.agent.open_door(py, px):\n                            if not 'locked' in self.agent.message:\n                                for _ in range(6):\n                                    if self.agent.open_door(py, px):\n                                        break\n                                else:\n                                    if kick_doors and not closed_shop:\n                                        while self.agent.glyphs[py, px] in G.DOOR_CLOSED:\n                                            self.agent.kick(py, px)\n                            else:\n                                if kick_doors and not closed_shop:\n                                    while self.agent.glyphs[py, px] in G.DOOR_CLOSED:\n                                        self.agent.kick(py, px)\n                    break\n\n","metadata":{"output":"    def explore1(self, search_prio_limit=0, door_open_count=4, kick_doors=True, trap_search_offset=0, check_altar_alignment=True, fast_go_to=False):\n        # TODO: refactor entire function\n\n\n        @Strategy.wrap\n        def open_neighbor_doors():\n            # TODO: polymorphed into a handless creature, too heavy load to kick, using lockpicks\n\n            yielded = False\n            # hypothesis: respecting the explicit shop-closure engraving avoids\n            # kicking down the locked door and provoking a lethal shopkeeper.\n            engraving = ''.join(c for c in self.agent.inventory.engraving_below_me.lower() if c.isalpha())\n            closed_shop = difflib.SequenceMatcher(None, engraving, 'closedforinventory').ratio() >= 0.55\n            for py, px in self.agent.neighbors(self.agent.blstats.y, self.agent.blstats.x, diagonal=False):\n                if (self.agent.current_level().door_open_count[py, px] < door_open_count or\n                        (kick_doors and not closed_shop)) and \\\n                        self.agent.glyphs[py, px] in G.DOOR_CLOSED:\n                    if not yielded:\n                        yielded = True\n                        yield True\n                    with self.agent.panic_if_position_changes():\n                        if not self.agent.open_door(py, px):\n                            if not 'locked' in self.agent.message:\n                                for _ in range(6):\n                                    if self.agent.open_door(py, px):\n                                        break\n                                else:\n                                    if kick_doors and not closed_shop:\n                                        while self.agent.glyphs[py, px] in G.DOOR_CLOSED:\n                                            self.agent.kick(py, px)\n                            else:\n                                if kick_doors and not closed_shop:\n                                    while self.agent.glyphs[py, px] in G.DOOR_CLOSED:\n                                        self.agent.kick(py, px)\n                    break\n\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace && sed -n '265,300p' autoascend/exploration_logic.py","time":{"start":1790541312028,"end":1790541312037}},"id":"prt_0e4943016001AUxs8fnCL0mSmJ","sessionID":"ses_f1b882f77ffebyKXRbssgjp7gn","messageID":"msg_0e493b48f001bFEG4nIkTYY4AL"}}
