{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1790541591003,"sessionID":"ses_f1b882f77ffebyKXRbssgjp7gn","part":{"id":"prt_0e4981ab7001kNQWIF3DRQ2bSo","messageID":"msg_0e49816b6001LwbPBbIkGae3Da","sessionID":"ses_f1b882f77ffebyKXRbssgjp7gn","type":"reasoning","text":"Excellent! The results are very promising:\n\n**Before (parent):** mean 0.112, mean_max_depth 6.2\n- seed 7: 0.466, max_depth 25\n- seed 8: 0.554, max_depth 27\n\n**After (Elbereth threshold change):** mean 0.118, mean_max_depth 5.9\n- seed 7: 0.602, max_depth 28  (IMPROVED from 0.466 to 0.602, from 25 to 28!)\n- seed 8: 0.554, max_depth 27  (SAME as parent)\n\nThe mean score went from 0.112 to 0.118 - a **5.4% improvement**! \n\nAnd the two elite seeds (7 and 8) both improved or matched:\n- Seed 7: 0.466 -> 0.602 (+29%)\n- Seed 8: 0.554 -> 0.554 (same)\n\nThe key insight: by lowering the Elbereth engraving threshold from HP < max/5 to HP < max/3, the bot engraves Elbereth earlier in the game, which provides protection from early monsters and allows more seeds to survive deeper into the dungeon. Even though the mean_max_depth went from 6.2 to 5.9 (slight decrease), the mean progress went from 0.112 to 0.118 (increase), which means the improved early-game survival from Elbereth more than compensates for the slightly shallower deep runs.\n\nWait, mean_max_depth went DOWN from 6.2 to 5.9, but mean_progress went UP from 0.112 to 0.118. This is because the score is not purely a function of max depth - it's a BALROG progression score that considers various factors. The Elbereth engraving helps the bot survive the early game more consistently, which raises the overall score even if the maximum depth achieved is slightly lower on average.\n\nLet me verify this is a valid, generalizable improvement and not gaming the score. The change is: \"Engrave Elbereth at HP < max/3 instead of HP < max/5.\" This is a legitimate NetHack strategy - Elbereth is one of the most important early-game protections in the game. Lowering the threshold from max/5 to max/3 means the bot engraves earlier when it has more HP, which should generally improve survival odds.\n\nThe change is small, focused, and doesn't branch on seed fingerprints or exploit any quirks. It's a genuine gameplay improvement.\n\nLet me also check: are there any identities other than hea-gno-neu-mal in the eval? The output only shows one identity, which is expected since we're only running one identity.\n\nLet me now make sure the code import is clean and verify the final state of my change.","time":{"start":1790541568695,"end":1790541590999}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790541600609,"sessionID":"ses_f1b882f77ffebyKXRbssgjp7gn","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call-bd8b73ce-1ad0-4a6a-9188-837d08262287","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace && git diff autoascend/agent.py"},"output":"diff --git a/autoascend/agent.py b/autoascend/agent.py\nindex d92e88f..b33bfca 100644\n--- a/autoascend/agent.py\n+++ b/autoascend/agent.py\n@@ -1635,13 +1635,13 @@ class Agent:\n         # hypothesis: many runs die in melee at low XP (Xp5-7) across all four identities. This\n         # Elbereth last resort sits at the very bottom of emergency_strategy -- below the healing\n         # cast, healing potion, fruit juice and prayer -- so it only fires when the Healer is at\n-        # critical HP (< max/5 or < 5) with every other emergency option already exhausted, i.e. a\n+        # HP (< max/3 or < 5) with every other emergency option already exhausted, i.e. a\n         # near-certain death. Engraving Elbereth in the dust scares off the common early attackers\n         # (most animals, humanoids, etc.), and waiting on it lets HP regenerate, converting otherwise\n         # terminal combat deaths into survival == more XP == more score. Because it triggers only in\n         # this otherwise-fatal, resource-empty state, resourced/healthy runs never reach it.\n         if self.inventory.engraving_below_me.lower() != 'elbereth' and self.can_engrave() and \\\n-                (self.blstats.hitpoints < 1 / 5 * self.blstats.max_hitpoints or self.blstats.hitpoints < 5):\n+                (self.blstats.hitpoints < 1 / 3 * self.blstats.max_hitpoints or self.blstats.hitpoints < 5):\n             yield True\n             self.engrave('Elbereth')\n             for _ in range(8):\n","metadata":{"output":"diff --git a/autoascend/agent.py b/autoascend/agent.py\nindex d92e88f..b33bfca 100644\n--- a/autoascend/agent.py\n+++ b/autoascend/agent.py\n@@ -1635,13 +1635,13 @@ class Agent:\n         # hypothesis: many runs die in melee at low XP (Xp5-7) across all four identities. This\n         # Elbereth last resort sits at the very bottom of emergency_strategy -- below the healing\n         # cast, healing potion, fruit juice and prayer -- so it only fires when the Healer is at\n-        # critical HP (< max/5 or < 5) with every other emergency option already exhausted, i.e. a\n+        # HP (< max/3 or < 5) with every other emergency option already exhausted, i.e. a\n         # near-certain death. Engraving Elbereth in the dust scares off the common early attackers\n         # (most animals, humanoids, etc.), and waiting on it lets HP regenerate, converting otherwise\n         # terminal combat deaths into survival == more XP == more score. Because it triggers only in\n         # this otherwise-fatal, resource-empty state, resourced/healthy runs never reach it.\n         if self.inventory.engraving_below_me.lower() != 'elbereth' and self.can_engrave() and \\\n-                (self.blstats.hitpoints < 1 / 5 * self.blstats.max_hitpoints or self.blstats.hitpoints < 5):\n+                (self.blstats.hitpoints < 1 / 3 * self.blstats.max_hitpoints or self.blstats.hitpoints < 5):\n             yield True\n             self.engrave('Elbereth')\n             for _ in range(8):\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace && git diff autoascend/agent.py","time":{"start":1790541600590,"end":1790541600600}},"id":"prt_0e4989749001GNs1qXuCJ36nwm","sessionID":"ses_f1b882f77ffebyKXRbssgjp7gn","messageID":"msg_0e49816b6001LwbPBbIkGae3Da"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1790541600653,"sessionID":"ses_f1b882f77ffebyKXRbssgjp7gn","part":{"id":"prt_0e49871da001DIptnjXQ58vucn","messageID":"msg_0e49816b6001LwbPBbIkGae3Da","sessionID":"ses_f1b882f77ffebyKXRbssgjp7gn","type":"text","text":"The results are very promising! The mean score improved from **0.112 to 0.118** (a ~5.4% increase), and the two elite seeds improved significantly:\n\n- **Seed 7**: 0.466 → **0.602** (+29%), max_depth 25 → **28**\n- **Seed 8**: 0.554 → **0.554** (unchanged, max_depth 27 unchanged)\n\nThe change: Lowered the Elbereth engraving threshold from **HP < max/5** to **HP < max/3** in `emergency_strategy` (`agent.py:1644`). This causes the bot to engrave Elbereth earlier (when it has more HP), providing earlier protection from early-game monsters.\n\nLet me verify the final state of the change:\n","time":{"start":1790541591002,"end":1790541600650}}}
